[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-001-authentication-modernization-pattern.md#after-oauth2oidc-authentication]

#### After (OAuth2/OIDC Authentication)

**User Experience:**

- Login once to Gainwell Identity Provider
- Access Enterprise™, Provider+™, Whole Health™ without re-login (SSO)
- Session timeout after 15 minutes of inactivity (HIPAA compliant)
- Activity tracking (mouse, keyboard, API calls reset timer)
- "Session expiring" warning at 14 minutes

**Technical Implementation:**

```typescript
// src/main.tsx
import { AuthProvider } from '@gainwell/auth';

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(
  <AuthProvider
    authority="https://identity.gainwell.com"
    clientId="gainwell-spa"
    scope="openid profile email api"
    sessionTimeout={900000} // 15 minutes (HIPAA)
  >
    <App />
  </AuthProvider>
);

// src/hooks/useAuthenticatedFetch.ts
export function useAuthenticatedFetch() {
  const { accessToken } = useAuth();

  return async (url: string, options?: RequestInit) => {
    const response = await fetch(url, {
      ...options,
      headers: {
        ...options?.headers,
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${accessToken}`
      }
    });

    // PHI access automatically logged by backend interceptor
    return response;
  };
}
```

**Benefits:**

- JWT tokens work with React SPAs
- SSO across all Gainwell products (single login)
- Stateless tokens scale to cloud (no server sessions)
- Automatic PHI access audit logging
- 15-minute timeout compliant with HIPAA
